TyrQuake v0.71 moved command registration into per-subsystem
*_AddCommands functions, but Commands_Init never calls NET_AddCommands,
and net.h no longer declares it. The listen, maxplayers, port and slist
console commands therefore do not exist. The Multiplayer menu's New Game
starts a server by queueing "listen 0", "maxplayers N" and "map ...";
only the map command runs, so it starts a one-player game that never
listens, and no other computer's search can find it. Only -listen on the
command line made a joinable server. Register the network commands with
the others. This is an upstream defect, independent of Kandelo.

Reference: pinned TyrQuake NQ/host.c Commands_Init, NQ/net_main.c
NET_AddCommands.

--- a/NQ/host.c
+++ b/NQ/host.c
@@ -807,6 +807,7 @@
     }
 
     SV_AddCommands();
+    NET_AddCommands();
 
     Cmd_AddCommand("game", Host_Gamedir_f);
     Cmd_SetCompletion("game", Host_Gamedir_Arg_f);
--- a/NQ/net.h
+++ b/NQ/net.h
@@ -259,6 +259,7 @@
 
 const char *NET_AdrToString(const netadr_t *a);
 
+void NET_AddCommands();
 void NET_RegisterVariables();
 void NET_Init();
 void NET_Shutdown();
